# Completion Review

## 2026-08-08

- Resolved the upstream `main` merge while preserving the fork search/FMO overlays,
  manual-only release workflow, and service-model manifest behavior.
- Renumbered fork FMO migrations from colliding `118–120` slots to `134–136`, with
  direct reconciliation for databases that recorded either `110–112` or `118–120`.
- Restored provider-manifest service injection with explicit exposure gating and
  canonical `cliproxy` storage IDs mapped to `cliproxyapi` manifest IDs.
- Reconciled upstream and fork search providers, removed stale explicit-`any`
  suppressions, and retained both unified `firecrawl` and fork `firecrawl-search`.
- Applied Code Simplifier cleanup to the conflict resolutions, including shared
  backend ID sets, explicit search result types, simpler You.com normalization,
  type-safe Firecrawl timestamp/filter handling, and formatter-clean migration
  directory discovery.
- Applied Code Simplifier cleanup to search hardening: explicit connection-ID
  resolution, non-nested Firecrawl base selection, direct proxy-context clearing,
  per-attempt proxy notes, and special-provider operation boundaries with
  category-aware Firecrawl content normalization; HTML payloads now use the
  schema-valid text content format and unknown/web categories normalize to the
  schema's `other` source type. HTTP error responses emit error proxy telemetry.
- Applied Code Simplifier cleanup to web-fetch routing: shared credential-provider
  mapping and keyless Mdream fixtures now preserve the canonical fallback order.
- Preserved web-fetch fallback for 401/transport failures while limiting 403
  fallback to registry-declared quota statuses, and hardened standalone script
  imports when launched from stdin/module test runners; the route now shares
  canonical Retry-After normalization for relative seconds, dates, and epoch-ms
  reset values while retaining the 300-second malformed-value default.
- Applied Code Simplifier cleanup to release workflow hardening: deterministic artifact
  provenance/candidate isolation, base-relative file-size coverage, release-rail ratchets,
  env-safe Docker channels with existing trigger topology preserved, manifest checks, and a
  blocking previous-version boot proof; quality scanner setup now resolves oasdiff from its
  official repository, requires pinned workflow scanners, and pins all external workflow
  actions. Self-target checks now distinguish same-name fork branches, while desktop verification
  requires both Intel/arm64 DMGs and exact updater manifests.

## 2026-07-08

- Fixed Docker build bundler override wiring: `OMNIROUTE_USE_TURBOPACK=0` is now a
  declared build arg before it becomes an image env var, so Shlink can build the
  upstream-synced commit with the webpack escape hatch instead of overloading the
  2-core host with Turbopack.

## 2026-07-04

- Added skip guards for Docker Hub publish when Docker credentials are missing and
  for Wiki Sync when the repository wiki is not enabled, preventing guaranteed-red
  GitHub Actions runs on `main`.
- Restored green CI gates for the FMO pool merge by documenting new env vars,
  re-exporting `fmoPools` through `localDb`, and reconciling current quality/file-size
  baselines already measured by CI.
- Fixed Parallel Extract credential resolution to use the valid `parallel-search`
  provider connection instead of the invalid `parallel` id, with shared-credential
  tests updated to match the managed provider contract.

## 2026-06-30

- Fixed post-archive shared fixture drift: `tests/fixtures/fmo/fmo-pools-v1.golden.json`
  now matches the FMO canonical fixture byte-for-byte (`quality_band.min/max` are
  `0.55`/`0.85`).
- Resolved upstream merge conflicts by keeping the Hermes ordered search chain while
  adding upstream `duckduckgo-free` fallback support and split provider/schema catalogs.
- Renumbered fork FMO migrations from colliding `100/101` slots to `110/111`,
  with compatibility reconciliation so old fork DBs do not skip upstream migrations.
- Restored web-fetch schema derivation from `webFetchRegistry` so Hermes providers
  (`mdream`, `parallel-extract`) and the `fallback` flag survive the upstream schema split.
- Moved fork-owned search providers behind `src/lib/search/providerRegistry.ts` and
  passed resolved search configs into `handleSearch`, keeping upstream
  `open-sse/config/searchRegistry.ts` free of Hermes provider entries.
